d 'EPIDEM': module providing suite of tools to detect outbreaks from surveillance data
d
d  epidem is a wrapper that provides a unified entry point for
d related tools: epidem channel – calls channel to construct the
d endemic channel using the average number of cases and its lower
d and upper	   historical limits in the corresponding week and
d adjacent weeks from previous (reference) years as cut points, and
d classifies	    each week as Baseline, Alarm, Alert, or
d Epidemic. epidem rregmm – calls rregmm to classify weeks in the
d evaluation year yeval using robust MM regression fitted to data
d from	      the ryspan preceding years.  epidem ppvalue – calls
d ppvalue to estimate, for a user-selected week and year, the
d posterior probability of a progressive	increase in cases
d over the next two weeks. 
d
d KW: epidemiology
d KW: surveillance
d KW: epidemic
d KW: prevalence
d
d Requires: Stata version 10 and robreg from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261104
d
d Author:  Leonelo Bautista,  University of Wisconsin at Madison
d Support: email  lebautista@@wisc.edu
d
f epidem.ado
f epidem.sthlp
f ../p/ppvalue.ado
f ../r/rregmm.ado
f ../c/channel.ado
f ../d/dengue_rd8.dta
f epidem_examples.do
